cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use arris in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "arris: a B-Rep geometric kernel in pure Rust"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sergienko
    given-names: Sergei
repository-code: "https://github.com/arris-labs/arris"
url: "https://github.com/arris-labs/arris"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  arris is a boundary-representation (B-Rep) geometric kernel written in
  pure Rust: analytic and NURBS geometry, tolerance-carrying topology,
  boolean operations that return provenance for every entity they touch,
  blends, sweeps and lofts, tessellation, and a STEP reader. Every result
  is checked for validity, every operation is deterministic, and every
  failure becomes a test fixture measured against an independent oracle.
  It ships as Rust crates and as the Python package arris.
keywords:
  - CAD
  - B-Rep
  - geometric kernel
  - solid modeling
  - NURBS
  - boolean operations
  - Rust
